How postfix aliases (language v0.18) are presented.

- A field alias x~(X) is kept as written, with its uses.
- A dual alias x~(K,V): uses of K are replaced by the label ("x"); V is kept.
- A pattern alias [string]~(K,_) is kept.
- A dynamic field's alias ("dy"+"n")~(K,V): the label is evaluated ("dyn"~(V)),
  but evaluated/raw/documented show uses of K as string, losing the value that
  final and data show ("dyn").
-- in.cue --
cases: {
	field:   {x~(X): 1, y: X}
	dual:    {x~(K, V): {n: 1}, y: K, z: V.n}
	pattern: {[string]~(K, _): {name: K}, foo: {}}
	dynamic: {("dy" + "n")~(K, V): {label: K}, w: V.label}
}
